issue.body:
Caused by: enabling `query_plan_optimize_join_order_limit=10` (measured: removing it removes the difference).

### Description

With query_plan_optimize_join_order_limit=10, a 4-table INNER JOIN over JSON columns (tables with automatic uniq statistics and a set skip index) is reordered so that a skewed 3M-row intermediate join result becomes the hash-join build side. The same query with the limit at 0 builds on base tables. The reordered plan runs about 2.8x slower and returns the same result.

Tested on `26.6.1.2244`: the SELECT succeeds without the settings and fails or differs with them.

### How to reproduce

Run the setup once, then run the SELECT as below, and again with the settings.

```sql
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS default.t1 SYNC;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS default.t2 SYNC;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS default.t3 SYNC;
CREATE TABLE default.t1 (`r` String, `j` JSON(k Array(String), sd Bool, ui Bool, rs Array(String), `a.t` String, `a.n` String, `a.ty` String, tid String) MATERIALIZED r, `Id` String, INDEX i1 j.k TYPE set(100) GRANULARITY 1) ENGINE = SharedMergeTree('/clickhouse/tables/{uuid}/{shard}', '{replica}') ORDER BY (j.sd, j.ui, j.a.ty, j.tid, Id) SETTINGS auto_statistics_types = 'minmax, uniq';
CREATE TABLE default.t2 (`r` String, `j` JSON(dn String, f1 Nullable(DateTime64(3)), f2 Nullable(DateTime64(3)), s Array(String), tid String, k Array(String)) MATERIALIZED r, `Id` String, INDEX i2 j.k TYPE set(100) GRANULARITY 1) ENGINE = SharedMergeTree('/clickhouse/tables/{uuid}/{shard}', '{replica}') ORDER BY (j.dn, Id) SETTINGS auto_statistics_types = 'minmax, uniq';
CREATE TABLE default.t3 (`r` String, `j` JSON(k Array(String)) MATERIALIZED r, `Id` String, INDEX i3 j.k TYPE set(100) GRANULARITY 1) ENGINE = SharedReplacingMergeTree('/clickhouse/tables/{uuid}/{shard}', '{replica}') ORDER BY (Id) SETTINGS auto_statistics_types = 'minmax, uniq';
INSERT INTO default.t1 (r, Id) SELECT concat('{"k":', if(number % 20 = 0, '["A","B"]', '["B"]'), ',"sd":false,"ui":true,"rs":["s1"],"a":{"t":"x', toString(number % 7), '","n":"n', toString(number % 1000), '","ty":"', if(number % 20 = 0, 'y0', 'y1'), '"},"tid":"z"}'), concat('e', toString(number)) FROM numbers(300000);
INSERT INTO default.t2 (r, Id) SELECT concat('{"eid":"e', toString((number % 3000) * 20), '","k":["C"],"s":["s1"],"st":"o","vid":"v', toString(number % 150000), '","f1":"2024-01-01 00:00:00","rv":["1.', toString(number % 9), '"],"f2":null,"dn":"d', toString(number % 5000), '","tid":"z"}'), concat('p', toString(number)) FROM numbers(3000000);
INSERT INTO default.t3 (r, Id) SELECT concat('{"k":["D"],"w":{"sev":"', ['l','m','h','c'][number % 4 + 1], '","s2":', toString((number % 100) / 10), ',"s3":', toString((number % 90) / 10), '},"sv":"h"}'), concat('v', toString(number)) FROM numbers(150000);
SELECT x0.j.a.t AS c1, x0.Id AS c2, x1.j.f1 AS c3, x1.j.rv AS c4, x1.j.f2 AS c5, x1.j.eid AS c6, x1.j.st AS c7, x1.Id AS c8, x2.j.sv AS c9, x2.j.w.s2 AS c10, x2.j.w.s3 AS c11, x2.Id AS c12, x3.j.a.t AS c13, x3.Id AS c14 FROM default.t1 AS x0 INNER JOIN default.t2 AS x1 ON (CAST(x1.j.eid, 'Nullable(String)') = x0.Id) AND ((has(CAST(x1.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'C') AND hasAny(x1.j.s, _CAST(['s0', 'all', 's1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 's5', 's6'], 'Array(String)'))) AND (x1.j.st = 'o')) INNER JOIN default.t3 AS x2 ON (CAST(x1.j.vid, 'Nullable(String)') = x2.Id) AND (has(CAST(x2.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'D') AND has(_CAST(['m', 'h', 'c'], 'Array(String)'), x2.j.w.sev)) INNER JOIN default.t1 AS x3 ON (CAST(x1.j.eid, 'Nullable(String)') = x3.Id) AND ((has(CAST(x3.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'B') AND (((x3.j.sd = _CAST('false', 'Bool')) AND (x3.j.ui = _CAST('true', 'Bool'))) AND hasAny(x3.j.rs, _CAST(['s0', 'all', 's1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 's5', 's6'], 'Array(String)')))) AND true) WHERE (has(CAST(x0.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'A') AND (((x0.j.sd = _CAST('false', 'Bool')) AND (x0.j.ui = _CAST('true', 'Bool'))) AND hasAny(x0.j.rs, _CAST(['s0', 's1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 'all'], 'Array(String)')))) AND true ORDER BY CAST(x0.j.a.n, 'Nullable(String)') ASC NULLS FIRST COLLATE 'en', CAST(x0.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST, CAST(x1.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST, CAST(x2.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST, CAST(x3.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 0, 31
SETTINGS compatibility = '26.4', join_use_nulls = '1', max_threads = '8', max_joined_block_size_rows = '1000', query_plan_optimize_join_order_limit = '0', transform_null_in = '1';
```

With the settings:

```sql
SELECT x0.j.a.t AS c1, x0.Id AS c2, x1.j.f1 AS c3, x1.j.rv AS c4, x1.j.f2 AS c5, x1.j.eid AS c6, x1.j.st AS c7, x1.Id AS c8, x2.j.sv AS c9, x2.j.w.s2 AS c10, x2.j.w.s3 AS c11, x2.Id AS c12, x3.j.a.t AS c13, x3.Id AS c14 FROM default.t1 AS x0 INNER JOIN default.t2 AS x1 ON (CAST(x1.j.eid, 'Nullable(String)') = x0.Id) AND ((has(CAST(x1.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'C') AND hasAny(x1.j.s, _CAST(['s0', 'all', 's1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 's5', 's6'], 'Array(String)'))) AND (x1.j.st = 'o')) INNER JOIN default.t3 AS x2 ON (CAST(x1.j.vid, 'Nullable(String)') = x2.Id) AND (has(CAST(x2.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'D') AND has(_CAST(['m', 'h', 'c'], 'Array(String)'), x2.j.w.sev)) INNER JOIN default.t1 AS x3 ON (CAST(x1.j.eid, 'Nullable(String)') = x3.Id) AND ((has(CAST(x3.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'B') AND (((x3.j.sd = _CAST('false', 'Bool')) AND (x3.j.ui = _CAST('true', 'Bool'))) AND hasAny(x3.j.rs, _CAST(['s0', 'all', 's1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 's5', 's6'], 'Array(String)')))) AND true) WHERE (has(CAST(x0.j.k, 'Array(String)'), 'A') AND (((x0.j.sd = _CAST('false', 'Bool')) AND (x0.j.ui = _CAST('true', 'Bool'))) AND hasAny(x0.j.rs, _CAST(['s0', 's1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 'all'], 'Array(String)')))) AND true ORDER BY CAST(x0.j.a.n, 'Nullable(String)') ASC NULLS FIRST COLLATE 'en', CAST(x0.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST, CAST(x1.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST, CAST(x2.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST, CAST(x3.Id, 'Nullable(String)') DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 0, 31
SETTINGS compatibility = '26.4', join_use_nulls = '1', max_threads = '8', max_joined_block_size_rows = '1000', query_plan_optimize_join_order_limit = '10', transform_null_in = '1';
```

### Performance

Original query (milliseconds; SQL omitted):

| 26.6.1.2244 without | 26.6.1.2244 with the settings | with/without |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 10523 | 28141 | 2.67× |

Synthetic repro above (milliseconds):

| Query | 26.6.1.2244 without | 26.6.1.2244 with the settings | with/without |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Query | 1432 | 4049 | 2.83× |

### Expected behavior

Enabling join reordering should not pick a plan that builds hash tables from the large intermediate result; runtime should stay close to the query_plan_optimize_join_order_limit=0 plan (about 1.4 s here).

