Thanks. I measured on the release binaries 26.7.6.57, 26.9.19.9, 26.10.2.103 and on current master; I did not build your head.

Declining `canBeExecutedOnDefaultArguments` on the consumer is what #117359 itself does for `parseDateTime`, so the two overrides look reasonable to me. Two things I would change:

1. The `+` / `-` shapes also regressed in 26.10 and are the more common spelling, so I would fix them here rather than in a follow-up. All of these return a value on 26.9.19.9 and throw `CANNOT_PARSE_DATETIME` on 26.10.2.103 and master:

```sql
SELECT max(formatDateTime(c1, '%Y-%m-%d 00:00:00') + INTERVAL 0 SECOND) FROM (SELECT parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(arrayJoin(['2026-01-01 10:00:00', '']), 3, 'UTC') AS c1);
SELECT max(formatDateTime(c1, '%Y-%m-%d 00:00:00') - INTERVAL 1 DAY) FROM (SELECT parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(arrayJoin(['2026-01-01 10:00:00', '']), 3, 'UTC') AS c1);
SELECT max(date_add(DAY, 1, formatDateTime(c1, '%Y-%m-%d 00:00:00'))) FROM (SELECT parseDateTime64BestEffortOrNull(arrayJoin(['2026-01-01 10:00:00', '']), 3, 'UTC') AS c1);
SELECT max(x + INTERVAL 0 SECOND) FROM (SELECT arrayJoin([NULL, '2026-01-01 10:00:00'])::Nullable(String) AS x);
```

`date_add` resolves to `plus` (the error names `FUNCTION plus`). From reading `FunctionBinaryArithmetic.h`, `plus` strips the Nullable itself and `executeDateTimeIntervalPlusMinus` calls the `addX` function on the non-Nullable nested column, so the new override cannot take effect on that path. Adding these queries to the test would confirm it either way.

2. The changelog entry calls the plain `Nullable(String)` case a regression from #117359, but it is older: `addDate(x, toIntervalSecond(0))` and `addSeconds(x, 0)` over `arrayJoin([NULL, '2026-01-01 10:00:00'])::Nullable(String)` already throw on 26.7.6.57 and 26.9.19.9. The new part in 26.10 is the `formatDateTime(...)` input and the plain `+ INTERVAL` case above. Fixing both here is fine, it is the same code; the entry should just say which part regressed.

`Bug Fix` looks right to me (valid input rejected in 26.10.2.103). I did not measure the cost of the filtered path for `Nullable(Date)` / `Nullable(DateTime)` with NULLs.

