comment.body:
Yes, it is a separate case that #130133 does not cover. #130133 parks the lease of a thread that waits in `ExternalLoader` for a dictionary being loaded on another thread. `dictGet` on a `direct` dictionary loads nothing: it runs the source pipeline on the thread that holds the outer slot, so that code is never reached.

Measured on a debug build of master `41a73dec` (contains #130133), and on the same commit with this PR's diff (`63412feb`) applied. Resource `(MASTER THREAD, WORKER THREAD)`, workload `max_concurrent_threads = 1`:

| Case | master | master + this PR |
|---|---|---|
| 05615 `direct` / `complex_key_direct` queries in `clickhouse local` (non-preemptive) | all 3 hang (killed at 40 s, `max_execution_time = 10` ignored) | pass, < 0.5 s |
| the same queries on a server with `cpu_slot_preemption = true` (default) | pass | pass |
| server with `cpu_slot_preemption = true`, `direct` dictionary whose source query takes more than one CPU quantum (repro below) | hangs, `max_execution_time = 15` ignored, `KILL QUERY ... SYNC` not done after 20 s | pass, 0.2 s |

So the preemptive variant you mention still reproduces after #130133, and once the source query outlives one quantum it is a full hang. The only executing thread is the outer query's, which holds the workload's one slot, and it waits in `CPULeaseAllocation::waitForGrant` <- `renew` <- `executeStepImpl` of the source query's executor, under `DirectDictionary::getColumns` <- `dictGet`. With this PR applied, the same repro completes.

```sql
CREATE RESOURCE cpu (MASTER THREAD, WORKER THREAD);
CREATE WORKLOAD all;
CREATE WORKLOAD one_slot IN all SETTINGS max_concurrent_threads = 1;
CREATE VIEW v_cpu AS SELECT number % 100 AS k, toString(sum(cityHash64(number))) AS v FROM numbers(20000000) GROUP BY k;
CREATE DICTIONARY d (k UInt64, v String) PRIMARY KEY k SOURCE(CLICKHOUSE(TABLE 'v_cpu')) LAYOUT(DIRECT());
SELECT sum(length(dictGet('d', 'v', number))) FROM numbers(3)
SETTINGS workload = 'one_slot', max_threads = 1, use_concurrency_control = 1, max_execution_time = 15;
```

One caveat for the test: `clickhouse local` never applies `cpu_slot_preemption`. Only `Server.cpp` calls `setCPUSlotPreemption`, and the `Context` default is `false`, so `system.server_settings` in local shows `0` even with `true` in the config. That means 05615 always runs non-preemptive and cannot cover the case above.

