issue.body:
### Company or project name

Malaa

### Describe what's wrong

A stored view that reads a session temporary table by its bare name works on 26.9 and breaks after the first server restart on 26.10.

`CREATE VIEW` leaves a table name unqualified when a temporary table of that name exists in the creating session. A later session resolves that bare name to its own temporary table. ClickHouse 26.10 qualifies those names while attaching the view from metadata. The attaching context has no session, so `AddDefaultDatabaseVisitor` rewrites `_lp_src` to `<view database>._lp_src`. A temporary table belongs to a session and not to a database, and a database-qualified name is not looked up among temporary tables. Every later query of the view fails with `UNKNOWN_TABLE`.

This cannot be shown on https://fiddle.clickhouse.com/ because the failure happens when the server loads the view from disk.

The production failure was an upgrade from 26.9.6 to 26.10.3.7. `26.10.3.7` has no public tag. The new load step is in `v26.10.2.103-stable` and is still present on `master` (`qualifyNamesFromLegacyMetadata` in `src/Databases/DatabaseOnDisk.cpp`, called from `createTableFromAST`). It is absent from `v26.9.6.6-stable`.

### Does it reproduce on the most recent release?

Yes

### How to reproduce

* Server: 26.10 (observed on 26.10.3.7; source checked at `v26.10.2.103-stable` and current `master`). The same script on 26.9.6 keeps working after the restart.
* Interface: clickhouse-client, one session for the setup, a new session after the restart.
* No non-default settings.

```sql
CREATE DATABASE repro;
CREATE TABLE repro.src (id UInt64) ENGINE = Memory;
INSERT INTO repro.src VALUES (1);

CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE _lp_src (id UInt64);
CREATE VIEW repro.v AS SELECT * FROM _lp_src;

-- same session: the bare name resolves to the temporary table
INSERT INTO _lp_src VALUES (1);
SELECT * FROM repro.v;
```

Restart the server, then in a new session:

```sql
CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE _lp_src ENGINE = Memory AS SELECT * FROM repro.src;
SELECT * FROM repro.v;
```

Before the restart, `SHOW CREATE VIEW repro.v` stores `FROM _lp_src`. After the restart the executed view body reads `repro._lp_src`.


### Expected behavior

The bare name stays bare across restart. `AddDefaultDatabaseVisitor` already refuses to qualify a name when the creating session has a temporary table of that name, and it refuses to qualify an `{name:Identifier}` parameter. Loading metadata should preserve that choice. The query after restart should return the row from the new session's `_lp_src`.

Qualifying the name with the view's database is the wrong repair here. The comment on `qualifyNamesFromLegacyMetadata` describes metadata written before CREATE-time qualification, in particular names introduced by SQL UDF expansion. A name that `CREATE VIEW` itself left unqualified, because a temporary table existed, is not that case. At startup `external_tables` is empty, so the visitor's temporary-table exception cannot fire, and every such name is rewritten.

### Error message and/or stacktrace

```text
Code: 60. DB::Exception: Unknown table expression identifier 'repro._lp_src'. (UNKNOWN_TABLE)
```

The production error had the same shape. The view lives in `lending_atomic_db`, and the query text after restart was:

```text
Code: 60. DB::Exception: Unknown table expression identifier
'lending_atomic_db._lp__stg__lending_views_v2__snap__lending_accounts'.
Maybe you meant lending_atomic_db.stg__lending_views_v2__snap__lending_accounts?
```

`CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` in a session that again holds the empty temporary table restores the bare name in memory. The next restart qualifies it again. Writing `repro._lp_src` into the view does not help: a qualified name is looked up only as a permanent table.


### Error message and/or stacktrace

_No response_

### Related issues and pull requests

Caused by: https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/114923
Related: https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/commit/3a1ae5bb46afb261490cb9b541a6f7987c762ead


### Additional context

We load one applicant's rows into session temporary tables and point the later views at those tables, so each stage runs once per applicant. A normal view is expanded again on every reference, and that expansion ran the same per-user logic hundreds of times per applicant and overloaded the warehouse.

src/Databases/DatabaseOnDisk.cpp (v26.10.2.103-stable and current master):

void qualifyNamesFromLegacyMetadata(ASTCreateQuery & ast_create_query, const String & database_name, ContextPtr context)
{
    // Metadata written before the table names were qualified at CREATE time ...
    if (ast_create_query.is_dictionary)
        return;

    AddDefaultDatabaseVisitor visitor(context, database_name);
    if (ast_create_query.select && ast_create_query.isView())
        visitor.visitTableExpressions(*ast_create_query.select);
    if (ast_create_query.columns_list)
        visitor.visitTableExpressions(*ast_create_query.columns_list);
}

createTableFromAST calls this for every definition read back from metadata. AddDefaultDatabaseVisitor skips an identifier that already has a database, that names a temporary table in external_tables, or that is a CTE alias. None of those apply at startup for a stored bare temporary-table name.

