issue.body:
Caused by: https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/117248 (automated bisect over master builds narrowed to its merge; the two adjacent candidate commits have no CI build, were built from source with the CI recipe and measured good)

### Description

On 26.10, a row policy that references currentUser() (e.g. `col = substring(currentUser(), ...)` on a sort-key column) is deferred past FINAL on ReplacingMergeTree, so PREWHERE is not used and every row of the table goes through FINAL merging before the policy filters it. 26.8 applied the same policy in PREWHERE before FINAL. In the repro, peak memory rises ~9.7x and time ~2.7x with identical results.

Regression between `26.8.1.672` (OLD) and `26.10.2.142` (NEW).

### How to reproduce

Run the setup once, then measure only the SELECT on each version.

```sql
CREATE TABLE default.t1 (`c1` String, `c2` String, `c4` String, `c5` DateTime, `c6` String, `c7` UInt8) ENGINE = ReplacingMergeTree(c5, c7) PARTITION BY c4 ORDER BY (c1, c2, c4);
INSERT INTO default.t1 SELECT toString(cityHash64(number)), if(number % 500 = 0, 'def', toString(number % 997)), ['a','b','c','d'][number % 4 + 1], toDateTime('2026-01-01 00:00:00') + number, concat('{"p":{"tags":["x","', if(number % 7 = 0, 'tag1', 'y'), '"],"t":"', repeat('z', 600), '"}}'), 0 FROM numbers(1500000);
INSERT INTO default.t1 SELECT toString(cityHash64(number)), if(number % 500 = 0, 'def', toString(number % 997)), ['a','b','c','d'][number % 4 + 1], toDateTime('2026-03-01 00:00:00') + number, concat('{"p":{"tags":["x","', if(number % 3 = 0, 'tag1', 'y'), '"],"t":"', repeat('z', 600), '"}}'), 0 FROM numbers(750000, 1500000);
CREATE ROW POLICY p1 ON default.t1 USING c2 = substring(currentUser(), 1, 3) TO default;
SELECT count() FROM default.t1 FINAL WHERE has(JSONExtract(c6, 'p', 'tags', 'Array(String)'), 'tag1')
SETTINGS compatibility = '24.0';
```

### Performance

Original query (milliseconds; SQL omitted):

| OLD 26.8.1.672 | NEW 26.10.2.142 | NEW/OLD |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 23716 | 37163 | 1.57× |

Synthetic repro above, peak memory in bytes of the SELECT (`system.query_log`; the measured regression):

| OLD 26.8.36.3 | NEW 26.10.3.7 | NEW/OLD |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 245,523,954 | 2,376,682,511 | 9.68× |

Synthetic repro above (milliseconds):

| OLD 26.8.36.3 | NEW 26.10.3.7 | NEW/OLD |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 27 | 74 | 2.74× |

### Expected behavior

A row policy that is deterministic within the query and depends only on ORDER BY columns should still be applied before FINAL (as documented for apply_row_policy_after_final), as in 26.8.

### Additional reproducers

Other findings with the same cause show it in different query shapes (27 findings with their own bisect, on one workload). Each repro is self-contained: run the setup once, then measure only the last `SELECT`.

#### A three-way join over such views and row policies

When tables are read through views with final=1 and have row policies that call currentUser(), a three-way join over ReplacingMergeTree tables uses much more memory and runs slower on 26.10 than on 26.8. On 26.10 the row-policy filter is no longer applied in PREWHERE before FINAL, so FINAL merges every row, including the large String column. The same policies written as literals do not regress.

```sql
CREATE TABLE default.t1 (`c1` String, `c2` String, `c3` String, `c5` DateTime, `c6` String, `c7` UInt8) ENGINE = ReplacingMergeTree(c5, c7) PARTITION BY c3 ORDER BY (c1, c2, c3);
INSERT INTO default.t1 SELECT lower(hex(SHA256(toString(number)))), if(number % 500 = 0, 'def', toString(number % 997)), ['s1','s2','s3','s4'][number % 4 + 1], toDateTime('2026-01-01 00:00:00') + number, concat('{"p":{"g":["a","g', toString(number % 5), '"],"n":"T', toString(number % 20), '","z":"', repeat('z', 1200), '"}}'), 0 FROM numbers(1500000);
INSERT INTO default.t1 SELECT lower(hex(SHA256(toString(number)))), if(number % 500 = 0, 'def', toString(number % 997)), ['s1','s2','s3','s4'][number % 4 + 1], toDateTime('2026-03-01 00:00:00') + number, concat('{"p":{"g":["a","g', toString(number % 3), '"],"n":"T', toString(number % 20), '","z":"', repeat('z', 1200), '"}}'), 0 FROM numbers(750000, 1500000);
CREATE TABLE default.t2 (`c2` String, `c1` FixedString(32), `c4` String, `c11` LowCardinality(String), `c5` DateTime, `c6` DateTime, `c12` Bool) ENGINE = ReplacingMergeTree(c6) ORDER BY (c2, c1);
INSERT INTO default.t2 SELECT if(number % 50 = 0, 'def', toString(number % 997)), toFixedString(lower(hex(MD5(toString(number)))), 32), ['d1','d2','d3'][intDiv(number, 7) % 3 + 1], ['k1','k2'][intDiv(number, 11) % 2 + 1], toDateTime('2026-01-01 00:00:00') + number * 60, now(), false FROM numbers(200000);
CREATE TABLE default.t3 (`c2` FixedString(32), `c8` FixedString(32), `c9` FixedString(64), `c10` String, `c13` Bool) ENGINE = ReplacingMergeTree ORDER BY (c2, c8, c9, c10);
INSERT INTO default.t3 SELECT toFixedString(if(number % 50 = 0, 'def', toString(number % 997)), 32), toFixedString(lower(hex(MD5(toString(number)))), 32), toFixedString(lower(hex(SHA256(toString(number * 10)))), 64), if(number % 13 = 0, 's2', 's1'), false FROM numbers(200000);
CREATE VIEW default.v1 AS SELECT * FROM default.t1 SETTINGS final = 1;
CREATE VIEW default.v2 AS SELECT x.* FROM default.t2 AS x SEMI LEFT JOIN default.t3 AS y ON (x.c1 = y.c8) AND (y.c13 = false) WHERE x.c12 = false SETTINGS final = 1;
CREATE VIEW default.v3 AS SELECT * FROM default.t3 SETTINGS final = 1;
CREATE ROW POLICY p1 ON default.t1 USING c2 = substring(currentUser(), 1, 3) TO default;
CREATE ROW POLICY p2 ON default.t2 USING c2 = substring(currentUser(), 1, 3) TO default;
CREATE ROW POLICY p3 ON default.t3 USING c2 = toFixedString(substring(currentUser(), 1, 3), 32) TO default;
SELECT c.c10, JSONExtractRaw(d.c6, 'p', 'g') AS r1, JSONExtractString(d.c6, 'p', 'n') AS r2, count() AS n FROM default.v3 AS c INNER JOIN default.v2 AS b ON b.c1 = c.c8 INNER JOIN default.v1 AS d ON d.c1 = c.c9 WHERE b.c4 = 'd1' GROUP BY c10, r1, r2 ORDER BY n DESC LIMIT 10
SETTINGS compatibility = '24.0';
